---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const reflowCss = `.responsive-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(
    auto-fit,
    minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr)
  );
  gap: var(--space-inline-md);
}

.responsive-grid > * {
  min-inline-size: 0;
}`;

const mediaCss = `.content {
  inline-size: min(100%, 70rem);
}

.content img,
.content video {
  max-inline-size: 100%;
  block-size: auto;
}

/* Avoid fixed heights: enlarged text needs to grow. */
.card {
  min-block-size: 12rem;
  block-size: auto;
}`;

const localScrollCss = `.table-scroll,
.code-scroll {
  max-inline-size: 100%;
  overflow-x: auto;
  overscroll-behavior-inline: contain;
}`;

const auditTs = `import { expect, test } from "@playwright/test";

const routes = ["/in", "/settings", "/checkout"];
const widths = [640, 320];

for (const route of routes) {
  for (const width of widths) {
    test(\`\${route} reflows at \${width}px\`, async ({ page }) => {
      await page.setViewportSize({ width, height: 900 });
      await page.goto(route);

      const hasPageOverflow = await page.evaluate(() => {
        const root = document.documentElement;
        return root.scrollWidth > root.clientWidth;
      });

      expect(hasPageOverflow).toBe(false);
      await expect(page.locator("main")).toBeVisible();
    });
  }
}`;
---

<Base
  title="Zoom y reflow"
  documentLayout="grid"
  description="Text at 200% and reflow at 400% without loss of content, controls or functionality."
>
  <h1>Zoom and reflow</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Zoom is not a visual preference or media query. It is a transformation of the viewport and the readable size: the content must wrap, the columns must stack, and all controls must remain available. The interface changes geometry, not capabilities.
  </p>

  <div class="sk-callout" data-tone="info">
    <div class="sk-callout__content">
      <p>
        <strong>200% and 400% test different contracts. </strong> At 200% it is verified that the text can grow without losing content or functionality. At 400% reflow is checked: a 1280px viewport is equivalent to <strong>320 CSS px</strong> and the page must be readable in only one direction.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two tests, two possible failures</h2>
  <div class="sk-table-scroll">
    <table class="sk-table">
      <thead class="sk-table__head">
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <th class="sk-table__header">Prueba</th>
          <th class="sk-table__header">What it requires</th>
          <th class="sk-table__header">Typical failure</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="sk-table__body">
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <td class="sk-table__cell"><strong>200%</strong></td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Readable text and operable controls</td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Labels cut by fixed heights</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <td class="sk-table__cell"><strong>400%</strong></td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Reflow a 320 CSS px</td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Columns or toolbars outside the viewport</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Layout retains capacity</h2>
  <p>
    This sample uses the same rule as a real card list. In wide width it has three columns; in the equivalent of 400% it converges into one. No cards disappear or change order.
  </p>

  <figure class="reflow-specimen">
    <div class="reflow-specimen__grid">
      <article class="sk-box" data-surface="surface" data-border="subtle" data-padding="md">
        <span class="reflow-specimen__index">01</span>
        <strong>Content</strong>
        <p>The text wraps and grows its own box.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="sk-box" data-surface="surface" data-border="subtle" data-padding="md">
        <span class="reflow-specimen__index">02</span>
        <strong>Controles</strong>
        <p>Actions remain visible and reachable.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="sk-box" data-surface="surface" data-border="subtle" data-padding="md">
        <span class="reflow-specimen__index">03</span>
        <strong>Orden</strong>
        <p>The DOM maintains a consistent reading sequence.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      The grid does not need a breakpoint per device: <code>auto-fit</code> responds to available space and <code>min(100%, 18rem)</code> prevents a column from imposing overflow.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <CodeBlock code={reflowCss} label="CSS · grid with reflow" />

  <h2>Implementation rules</h2>

  <h3>Let text and media grow</h3>
  <p>
    Avoid fixed heights in boxes with content. Images and video are limited to the available width without distorting their proportion.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={mediaCss} label="CSS · flexible content" />

  <h3>Horizontal scrolling is local, not global</h3>
  <p>
    Data tables, code, maps and diagrams may require two dimensions. The scroll belongs to that component; the title, the explanation and the rest of the page continue to reflow.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={localScrollCss} label="CSS · overflow local" />

  <h2>How to ensure it in your system</h2>

  <h3>1. Make the container decide</h3>
  <p>
    A component should not know the width of the device. Give it a flexible width, allow its children to shrink with <code>min-inline-size: 0</code>, and let the container change columns, wrapping, or layout based on actual space.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Defines one reflow contract per component</h3>
  <div class="sk-table-scroll">
    <table class="sk-table">
      <thead class="sk-table__head">
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <th class="sk-table__header">Tipo</th>
          <th class="sk-table__header">Minimum contract</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="sk-table__body">
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Text, Callout, Tile, Card</td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Automatic height; labels and content can wrap.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Navbar y toolbar</td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Actions wrap, change rows, or move to an accessible menu.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Dialog, Drawer y popover</td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Head into the viewport; The bodysuit has internal scrolling if necessary.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Grid y Stack</td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Columns converge without changing the order of the DOM.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="sk-table__row">
          <td class="sk-table__cell">Table, code, map</td>
          <td class="sk-table__cell">The horizontal overflow is contained in the component.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>3. Audit all paths</h3>
  <p>
    Run a matrix with each path and the effective widths of 200% and 400%. This test detects global overflow automatically; It adds to each flow its essential interactions because a visible interface may still have lost functionality.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={auditTs} label="Playwright reflow matrix" lang="ts" />

  <h3>4. Finish with real zoom</h3>
  <p>
    An automated narrow viewport tests the geometry, but does not replace the final review: open the browser at 200% and 400%, navigate the page with the keyboard and test menus, dialogs, tooltips, validations and states with long content.
  </p>

  <h2>What breaks with fixed zoom</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>width</code> or <code>min-width</code> larger than the effective viewport.</li>
    <li><code>height</code> fixed on buttons, cards, callouts or fields with text.</li>
    <li><code>white-space: nowrap</code> in labels that do not have a responsive output.</li>
    <li>Toolbars that hide actions instead of wrapping or rearranging them.</li>
    <li>Positioned content with physical offsets that stops participating in the flow.</li>
    <li><code>overflow: hidden</code> used to hide the symptom instead of fixing the width.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Documentation Site Contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      At 200%, the effective 640 px CSS layout does not produce global horizontal scrolling.
    </li>
    <li>
      At 400%, the effective 320 px CSS layout stacks the content in one column.
    </li>
    <li>
      The header goes to two rows: identity on top; search and preferences below.
    </li>
    <li>
      Menu, search, palette, theme and contrast remain visible and operable.
    </li>
    <li>
      Code blocks and tables contain their own overflow when needed.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Test text at 200%, not just a mobile viewport.</li>
    <li>Test 400% from 1280px or directly to 320 CSS px.</li>
    <li>Read the entire page using only vertical scrolling.</li>
    <li>Opens menus, dialogs and popovers; visible does not mean operable.</li>
    <li>Change theme and preferences to detect overlapping controls.</li>
    <li>Confirms that focus and reading order follow the visual order.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Referencias:
    <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/resize-text.html">
      WCAG 1.4.4 Resize Text
    </a>
    y
    <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/reflow.html">
      WCAG 1.4.10 Reflow
    </a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .reflow-specimen {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-stack-sm);
    margin: var(--space-stack-md) 0 var(--space-section);
  }

  .reflow-specimen__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(
      auto-fit,
      minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr)
    );
    gap: var(--space-inline-md);
    padding: var(--space-inset-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-surface);
    background: var(--color-bg-surface-sunken);
  }

  .reflow-specimen__grid article {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-stack-xs);
    min-inline-size: 0;
    align-content: start;
  }

  .reflow-specimen__grid p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .reflow-specimen__index {
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .reflow-specimen figcaption {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    line-height: var(--font-line-height-caption);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
</style>
